\title{Merkle Trees and Vector Commitments}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The commitment underneath every hash-based system. Simple enough that it is easy to skip and consequential enough that the [hash choice](dhsorens-0048) dominates prover time.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Position binding, and what a Merkle commitment does not give you.}
        \li{Batched openings and path deduplication; where proof size actually goes.}
        \li{Salting and its role in [zero knowledge](dhsorens-002E) — and in ArkLib's \code{Salt.lean}.}
        \li{[Hash cost as the prover's real bottleneck](dhsorens-004D); arity and tree shape tradeoffs.}
        \li{The formalisation: what ArkLib's Merkle tree development proves, and what it assumes about the hash.}
    }
}
